          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I have been getting heartburn most evenings.",
          "answer": "Your symptoms of heartburn experienced most evenings are classified as needing **routine** care. This means you should seek medical advice, especially if the symptoms worsen or are new and unexplained.\n\nHeartburn is commonly associated with gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD). The typical presentation includes a burning sensation behind the breastbone and may involve regurgitation of acid or food. Factors that can contribute to heartburn include excess body weight, large or late meals, smoking, alcohol consumption, pregnancy, and certain medications (General clinical reference on GERD).\n\nSince your symptoms are occurring regularly, it could be helpful to discuss this pattern with a healthcare provider. They might want to investigate lifestyle factors or consider treatment options for GERD. Other potential causes of heartburn can include anxiety or dietary triggers, which could also be worth exploring with a clinician.\n\nIf you notice any severe symptoms or changes, do not hesitate to seek care sooner.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
